# app/graphql - GraphQL API (generated by rakitin)

GraphQL over HTTP endpoint backed by [graphql-http](https://github.com/graphql/graphql-http).

## Mount

```js
const { mountGraphQL } = require("./app/graphql");

mountGraphQL(app);                  // POST/GET /graphql
mountGraphQL(app, "/api/graphql");  // custom base path
```

## Files

| File | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `index.js` | Loads the SDL, exports `schema`, `rootValue`, `mountGraphQL`, `graphql()` |
| `schema.graphql` | SDL - root types plus the rakitin-managed per-module region |
| `resolvers.js` | `rootValue` map - service calls live in the managed region |

## Expose a module

```bash
rakitin add graphql --module user
```

This appends the module's type, queries and mutations into both managed
regions (`# rakitin:graphql:start|end` in the SDL, `// rakitin:graphql:start|end`
in the resolvers). Re-running the same command changes nothing, and every byte
outside the markers is preserved.

## Example

```graphql
query {
  userList(page: 1, limit: 10) {
    items { id name }
    total
  }
}
```
